# Code Standards

## TypeScript

- `strict: true` in all tsconfig files
- No `any` — use `unknown` + type guards
- Prefer `interface` for object shapes, `type` for unions/intersections
- Export types from `packages/shared`, never duplicate

## Naming

| Kind | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Files | kebab-case | `merchant-profile.service.ts` |
| Classes | PascalCase | `MerchantProfileService` |
| Functions | camelCase | `claimBinding` |
| Constants | SCREAMING_SNAKE | `MAX_COMMISSION_RATE` |
| DB columns | camelCase (Prisma) | `onboardingStatus` |
| API routes | kebab-case | `/api/v1/merchant/onboarding` |

## NestJS

- One module per domain: `*.module.ts`, `*.controller.ts`, `*.service.ts`
- DTOs in `dto/` subfolder with `class-validator` decorators
- Services contain business logic; controllers are thin
- Use `PrismaService` — no raw SQL without justification

## Next.js

- Server Components by default
- `'use client'` only for interactivity (forms, modals, QR scanner)
- Colocate feature components: `app/(crm)/contacts/_components/`
- API client in `lib/api/` per app

## Error Handling

```typescript
// API: consistent error shape
throw new BadRequestException({
  message: 'Validation failed',
  details: [{ field: 'email', message: 'Invalid email' }],
});
```

- Log errors server-side; never expose stack traces in production
- Frontend: toast for transient errors, inline for form validation

## Git Commits

Format: `type(scope): description`

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `refactor`, `test`, `chore`

## Testing

- Unit: `*.spec.ts` / `*.test.ts`
- API integration: Supertest in `apps/api/test/`
- E2E: Playwright in `e2e/`
- Map every P0 acceptance criterion to a test

## Imports

```typescript
// Order: external → @meridian/* → relative
import { Injectable } from '@nestjs/common';
import { OnboardingStatus } from '@meridian/shared';
import { PrismaService } from '../prisma/prisma.service';
```
